UniqueViolation: a row with this key is already there
ForeignKeyViolation: the row it points at is missing, or something still points at this one
NotNullViolation: a column that needs a value was left empty
CheckViolation: a rule written into the table refused the row
Deadlock: two transactions each waited for the other, and this one was picked to lose
SerializationFailure: another transaction changed the same rows first
ConnectionLost: the connection is gone
Timeout: it ran too long and was cancelled
Syntax: the server will not run that statement at all
Permission: this login may not do that
Other: anything the driver has no case of its own for
